    "answer": "### PHYSICAL QUALITY OF LIFE INDEX (PQLI)\nDeveloped by Morris D. Morris, PQLI is a non-monetary composite index measuring the quality of life or social well-being.\n* **Three Indicators**:\n  1. **Infant Mortality Rate (IMR)**: Reflects clean water, nutrition, and home environment.\n  2. **Life Expectancy at Age 1**: Represents general healthcare availability and nutrition.\n  3. **Basic Literacy Rate**: Reflects education, economic capability, and social awareness.\n* **Scoring System**: Each indicator is rated on a scale of **1 to 100** (where 1 is the worst performance and 100 is the best). \n* **Calculation**: PQLI is the simple arithmetic mean of the three indicators.\n  $$\\text{PQLI} = \\frac{\\text{IMR Index} + \\text{Life Expectancy Index} + \\text{Literacy Rate}}{3}$$",
