    "answer": "### HUMAN DEVELOPMENT INDEX (HDI)\nDeveloped by the UNDP (United Nations Development Programme), HDI is a composite statistical index of social and economic development.\n* **Three Key Dimensions & Indicators**:\n  1. **Long and Healthy Life**: Measured by **Life Expectancy at Birth**.\n  2. **Knowledge (Education)**: Composite of:\n     * *Mean years of schooling* for adults aged 25+.\n     * *Expected years of schooling* for children entering school.\n  3. **Decent Standard of Living**: Measured by **Gross National Income (GNI) per capita** adjusted for Purchasing Power Parity (PPP$).\n* **Calculation**:\n  * Each dimension is indexed between 0 and 1.\n  * HDI is the **Geometric Mean** of the three dimension indices:\n    $$\\text{HDI} = \\sqrt[3]{\\text{Health Index} \\times \\text{Education Index} \\times \\text{Income Index}}$$",
