    "chapter": "Concepts of Health and Disease",
    "stars": 3,
    "answer": "### SULLIVAN'S INDEX (DISABILITY-FREE LIFE EXPECTANCY)\nSullivan's Index is a highly sensitive and advanced composite health indicator that measures the quality of life, rather than just the quantity (expectancy) of life.\n* **Definition**: It represents the number of years a person is expected to live in a completely healthy, disability-free state.\n* **Calculation Method**:\n  $$\\text{Sullivan's Index} = \\text{Life Expectancy at Birth} - \\text{Duration of Bed Disability/Inactivity}$$\n* **Epidemiological Importance**:\n  * While traditional \"Life Expectancy\" has increased globally due to medical progress, people are often living longer with chronic illness and disability.\n  * Sullivan's Index helps policy-makers evaluate whether health programs are truly adding \"healthy years to life\" rather than just \"adding years to chronic sickness\".",
