    "id": 45,
    "text": "Add a note on ADVERSE EVENTS FOLLOWING IMMUNIZATION(AEFI).",
    "type": "SAQ",
    "chapter": "Epidemiology (Principles & Methods)",
    "stars": 3,
    "answer": "### ADVERSE EVENTS FOLLOWING IMMUNIZATION (AEFI)\nAn AEFI is any untoward medical occurrence which follows immunization and which does not necessarily have a causal relationship with the usage of the vaccine. It can be any unfavorable or unintended sign, abnormal laboratory finding, symptom, or disease.\n\n#### WHO Classification of AEFI\n1.  **Vaccine Product-Related Reaction**:\n    *   *Cause*: Triggered by the vaccine due to one or more inherent properties of the vaccine product.\n    *   *Examples*: Fever, local pain, swelling at injection site, febrile seizures, vaccine-induced thrombocytopenia.\n2.  **Vaccine Quality Defect-Related Reaction**:\n    *   *Cause*: Caused by a vaccine due to one or more quality defects of the vaccine product, including its administration device provided by the manufacturer.\n    *   *Examples*: Failure of attenuation in live vaccine, contamination of a batch.\n3.  **Immunization Error-Related Reaction (Programmatic Error)**:\n    *   *Cause*: Caused by inappropriate vaccine handling, prescribing, or administration.\n    *   *Examples*: Non-sterile injection (leading to abscess), reconstitution with the wrong diluent (leading to toxic shock syndrome), incorrect dose or route.\n4.  **Immunization Anxiety-Related Reaction**:\n    *   *Cause*: Arising from anxiety about, or pain of, immunization.\n    *   *Examples*: Vasovagal syncope, hyperventilation, headache, dizziness.\n5.  **Coincidental Event**:\n    *   *Cause*: An event that occurs after immunization but is caused by something other than the vaccine or its administration (e.g., a child developing malaria or viral fever shortly after vaccination).\n\n#### Surveillance and Reporting\nAll AEFIs must be documented, and serious AEFIs (death, life-threatening, hospitalization, permanent disability) must be reported immediately (within 24 hours) through the national AEFI surveillance system for investigation and causality assessment.",
    "page": 5
