    "text": "Add a note on National Immunization Schedule.",
    "type": "SAQ",
    "chapter": "Epidemiology (Principles & Methods)",
    "stars": 6,
    "answer": "### NATIONAL IMMUNIZATION SCHEDULE (NIS) IN INDIA\nThe National Immunization Schedule (NIS) in India, implemented under the Universal Immunization Programme (UIP), protects infants, children, and pregnant women from vaccine-preventable diseases.\n\n#### 1. For Pregnant Women\n*   **Td-1 (Tetanus & adult Diphtheria)**: Early in pregnancy. (0.5 ml, IM, Upper arm).\n*   **Td-2**: 4 weeks after Td-1. (0.5 ml, IM, Upper arm).\n*   **Td-Booster**: If pregnant within 3 years of receiving 2 Td doses in a previous pregnancy. (0.5 ml, IM, Upper arm).\n\n#### 2. For Infants (up to 1 year)\n*   **BCG**: At birth (or up to 1 year). (0.05 ml up to 1 month, then 0.1 ml; Intradermal; Left upper arm).\n*   **Hepatitis B (Birth dose)**: Within 24 hours of birth. (0.5 ml, IM, Anterolateral aspect of mid-thigh).\n*   **OPV-0**: At birth (within 15 days). (2 drops, Oral).\n*   **OPV-1, 2, 3**: At 6, 10, 14 weeks. (2 drops, Oral).\n*   **Pentavalent (DPT + HepB + Hib) 1, 2, 3**: At 6, 10, 14 weeks. (0.5 ml, IM, Anterolateral aspect of mid-thigh).\n*   **Rotavirus Vaccine (RVV)**: At 6, 10, 14 weeks. (5 drops or 2.5 ml oral depending on vaccine type).\n*   **Fractional IPV (fIPV)**: At 6 and 14 weeks. (0.1 ml, Intradermal, Right upper arm).\n*   **Pneumococcal Conjugate Vaccine (PCV)**: At 6 weeks, 14 weeks, and Booster at 9 completed months. (0.5 ml, IM, Anterolateral aspect of mid-thigh).\n*   **MR (Measles-Rubella) 1st dose**: At 9 completed months to 12 months. (0.5 ml, Subcutaneous, Right upper arm).\n*   **JE (Japanese Encephalitis) 1st dose**: At 9 completed months to 12 months (in endemic districts). (0.5 ml, Subcutaneous, Left upper arm/IM depending on vaccine type).\n*   **Vitamin A (1st dose)**: At 9 months with MR-1. (1 lakh IU = 1 ml, Oral).\n\n#### 3. For Children (1 to 16 years)\n*   **MR 2nd dose**: At 16-24 months. (0.5 ml, Subcutaneous).\n*   **JE 2nd dose**: At 16-24 months. (0.5 ml, Subcutaneous).\n*   **DPT Booster-1**: At 16-24 months. (0.5 ml, IM, Anterolateral thigh).\n*   **OPV Booster**: At 16-24 months. (2 drops, Oral).\n*   **Vitamin A (2nd to 9th dose)**: 2nd dose at 16-18 months, then every 6 months up to 5 years of age. (2 lakh IU = 2 ml, Oral).\n*   **DPT Booster-2**: At 5-6 years. (0.5 ml, IM, Upper arm).\n*   **Td**: At 10 years and 16 years. (0.5 ml, IM, Upper arm).",
