    "text": "Define Health information and Biostatistics.",
    "type": "SAQ",
    "chapter": "Biostatistics & Health Information",
    "stars": 1,
    "answer": "### HEALTH INFORMATION AND BIOSTATISTICS\n\n#### 1. Health Information\n*   **Definition**: Health Information is the processed data that is used for planning, managing, and evaluating health services. It refers to the systematic collection, analysis, and interpretation of health-related data to improve health outcomes and health system performance.\n*   **Sources of Health Information**:\n    1.  *Census*: Conducted every 10 years in India.\n    2.  *Civil Registration System (CRS)*: Compulsory permanent registration of vital events (births, deaths).\n    3.  *Sample Registration System (SRS)*: Provides annual estimates of vital rates.\n    4.  *Disease Notification, Hospital Records, and Health Surveys* (e.g., NFHS).\n\n#### 2. Biostatistics\n*   **Definition**: Biostatistics is the branch of statistics applied to biological and medical sciences. It involves the application of statistical methods for collecting, organizing, summarizing, analyzing, and drawing inferences from data related to medicine, biology, public health, and clinical research.\n*   **Key Uses in Public Health**:\n    *   To define what is normal in a population by calculating parameters (e.g., normal blood pressure, height, weight).\n    *   To test the efficacy of a new drug or vaccine (using tests of significance like t-test, Chi-square test).\n    *   To study the association between risk factors and diseases in epidemiological studies.\n    *   To assess health trends in a population.",
