    "answer": "### SLOW SAND FILTRATION (BIOLOGICAL/ENGLISH FILTER)\nA highly effective method of purifying large water volumes using biological processes.\n* **Structure & Components**:\n  1. **Supernatant Water Reservoir**: Provides a constant head of water (1-1.5 meters) above the sand.\n  2. **Sand Bed**: 1-meter-deep bed of graded sand.\n  3. **Schmutzdecke (Vital Layer / Biological Layer)**: A slimy, gelatinous layer of algae, bacteria, and protozoa that forms on top of the sand within a few days. **This is the heart of slow sand filtration**, biologically consuming pathogens and filtering impurities.\n  4. **Under-drain System**: Collects the filtered water.",
