    "text": "Add a note on swachh Bharat",
    "type": "SAQ",
    "chapter": "Environment and Health",
    "stars": 4,
    "answer": "### Swachh Bharat Abhiyan (Clean India Mission)\n**Swachh Bharat Abhiyan** is a country-wide cleanliness and sanitation campaign launched by the Government of India. It is recognized as one of the largest public health and sanitation initiatives in modern history.\n\n#### 1. Launch and Core Target\n*   **Launch Date**: Launched on **2nd October 2014** (marking the 145th birth anniversary of Mahatma Gandhi) by Prime Minister Narendra Modi.\n*   **Primary Goal**: To achieve an **Open Defecation Free (ODF) India** by **2nd October 2019** (the 150th birth anniversary of Mahatma Gandhi) through the rapid construction of individual and community sanitary latrines.\n\n#### 2. Core Objectives\n*   Eliminate the practice of open defecation.\n*   Eradicate the practice of manual scavenging.\n*   Introduce modern, scientific systems for **Municipal Solid and Liquid Waste Management**.\n*   Bring about a sustainable behavioral change regarding healthy sanitation practices.\n*   Create awareness about the direct link between sanitation, environmental hygiene, and public health.\n\n#### 3. The Two Sub-Missions\nThe campaign was structured into two operational divisions:\n*   **Swachh Bharat Mission (Gramin/Rural)**: Managed by the Ministry of Drinking Water and Sanitation (now the Ministry of Jal Shakti). Focused on constructing household toilets in rural villages, eliminating open defecation, and mobilizing rural communities.\n*   **Swachh Bharat Mission (Urban)**: Managed by the Ministry of Housing and Urban Affairs. Focused on building community toilets, public toilets, and improving municipal solid waste management in towns and cities.\n\n#### 4. Swachh Bharat Mission 2.0 (Phase II)\n*   Launched for the period **2020-21 to 2024-25**.\n*   The focus has shifted from merely achieving ODF status to sustaining it and transitioning to **ODF Plus (ODF+) and ODF++**.\n*   *ODF+*: Focuses on toilet functionality and water availability.\n*   *ODF++*: Emphasizes complete safe management of fecal sludge (sewage treatment), plastic waste management, and greywater management.",
    "page": 11
