    "text": "Add a note on MID DAY MEAL PROGRAM.",
    "type": "SAQ",
    "chapter": "Nutrition and Health",
    "stars": 4,
    "answer": "### The Mid-Day Meal Program (PM POSHAN)\n\nOriginally launched in 1995 as the *National Programme of Nutritional Support to Primary Education*, this initiative was renamed **PM POSHAN (Pradhan Mantri Poshan Shakti Nirman)** in 2021. It is a centrally sponsored scheme that provides hot, cooked meals to school children.\n\n#### 1. Core Objectives\n*   To improve the nutritional status of school-age children.\n*   To increase school enrollment, attendance, and retention rates, particularly among girls and underprivileged children.\n*   To foster social integration and remove caste barriers by having children sit and eat together.\n\n#### 2. Target Beneficiaries\nChildren in classes I to VIII studying in government schools, government-aided schools, local body schools, and education centers supported under the Samagra Shiksha scheme.\n\n#### 3. Nutritional Standards (Daily Norms per Child)\nThe meals are designed to meet specific energy and protein requirements:\n\n| Parameter | Primary (Classes I - V) | Upper Primary (Classes VI - VIII) |\n| :--- | :--- | :--- |\n| **Energy** | At least 450 Calories | At least 700 Calories |\n| **Protein** | 12 grams | 20 grams |\n| **Food grains** | 100 grams | 150 grams |\n| **Pulses** | 20 grams | 30 grams |\n| **Vegetables** | 50 grams | 75 grams |\n| **Oil & Fat** | 5 grams | 7.5 grams |\n\nAdditionally, the program is integrated with the weekly iron and folic acid supplementation (IFA pink/blue tablets) and deworming initiatives.\n\n#### 4. Operational Guidelines and Quality Control\n*   **Freshness:** The meal must be cooked fresh on school premises or in designated centralized kitchens, and served hot.\n*   **Hygiene standards:** Safe storage of raw materials, clean drinking water for cooking, and mandatory hand hygiene for kitchen staff and children.\n*   **Food Safety Testing:** Random food samples must be tested by accredited laboratories to ensure quality and caloric value.\n*   **Community Participation:** Encourages mothers' self-help groups (SHGs) and School Management Committees (SMC) to monitor the cooking and serving of meals.",
