    "text": "Add a note on FLUOROSIS(Endemic Fluorosis). {Write about Nalgonda technique}",
    "type": "SAQ",
    "chapter": "Nutrition and Health",
    "stars": 5,
    "answer": "### 1. ENDEMIC FLUOROSIS\nEndemic fluorosis is a chronic disease caused by excess intake of fluoride, primarily through drinking water containing fluoride $> 1.5\\text{ mg/l}$.\n* **Clinical Manifestations**:\n  1. **Dental Fluorosis**: Mottling of teeth, yellow/brown staining, pitting of enamel. Occurs in children.\n  2. **Skeletal Fluorosis**: Severe bone changes, osteosclerosis, calcification of ligaments. Leads to joint pain, rigid spine, and \"genu valgum\" (knock-knees).\n* **THE NALGONDA TECHNIQUE (DE-FLUORIDATION METHOD)**:\n  Developed by NEERI in India, this is an economical chemical method to remove excess fluoride from drinking water using **Alum (coagulation)** and **Lime (pH adjustment/flocculation)** followed by sedimentation.",
