    "text": "add a note on EUTHENICS(3marks)",
    "type": "SAQ",
    "chapter": "Genetics, Mental Health & Social Medicine",
    "stars": 1,
    "answer": "### Euthenics\n\n**Euthenics** is defined as the science and study of improving human functioning, well-being, and phenotypic expression through the optimization of living conditions and the external environment.\n\n#### 1. Core Philosophy\nWhile **Eugenics** focuses on altering the genotype (genetic makeup) to improve the species, **Euthenics** focuses on optimizing the **phenotype** (how genes are expressed) by altering the environment. It operates on the principle that \"even the best genetic potential cannot be realized without a healthy, nurturing, and clean environment.\"\n\n#### 2. Practical Applications of Euthenics in Public Health:\n\n*   **Nutritional Intervention:** Providing adequate protein-energy nutrition and micronutrients to pregnant women and young children (e.g., ICDS, PM POSHAN) to prevent stunting, cognitive impairment, and physical developmental delay.\n*   **Environmental Control:** Improving housing standards, ensuring a safe water supply, and providing proper sanitation to eliminate infectious disease transmission and environmental toxicity.\n*   **Education and Early Stimulation:** Universal education and intellectually stimulating environments in early childhood to maximize cognitive potential.\n*   **Preventive Medicine:** Comprehensive immunization programs and regular health check-ups to protect growing children from debilitating illnesses, allowing them to achieve their full genetic potential.",
    "page": 16
