    "id": 185,
    "text": "A)Enlist Sexually Transmitted Infections (STIs) B)Describes Syndromic Management Of Reproductive Tract Infections Or Sexually Transmitted Infections (RTI/STI ) + HIV / AIDS  A.Epidemiology B. Problem Statement C.Who Clinical Staging Of HIV . D.HIV-TB Co-Infection. E. Chemoprophylaxis. F.Add A Note On NACO Program.",
    "type": "SAQ",
    "chapter": "Epidemiology of Communicable Diseases",
    "stars": 12,
    "answer": "### SEXUALLY TRANSMITTED INFECTIONS (STIs)\n\n### A) ENUMERATION OF COMMON STIs\n1. **Bacterial**: Gonorrhoea (*N. gonorrhoeae*), Syphilis (*T. pallidum*), Chlamydia (*C. trachomatis*), Chancroid (*H. ducreyi*).\n2. **Viral**: HIV/AIDS, Genital Herpes (HSV-2), Genital Warts/HPV, Hepatitis B.\n3. **Parasitic**: Trichomoniasis (*Trichomonas vaginalis*), Pediculosis pubis, Scabies.\n\n### B) SYNDROMIC MANAGEMENT OF STIs (NACO Guidelines)\nSyndromic management is a **clinical approach** to treating STIs based on the patient's symptoms and signs, without waiting for laboratory confirmation. It uses pre-designed flowcharts (algorithms) for common STI syndromes.\n\n**Common Syndromes and Treatment**:\n| Syndrome | Common Causes | Treatment |\n|---|---|---|\n| **Urethral Discharge (Male)** | Gonorrhoea, Chlamydia | Cefixime 400 mg PO single dose + Doxycycline 100 mg BD × 7 days |\n| **Vaginal Discharge** | *Trichomonas*, Bacterial Vaginosis, Candida | Metronidazole 400 mg BD × 7 days + Fluconazole |\n| **Genital Ulcer Disease** | Syphilis, Herpes, Chancroid | Benzathine Penicillin IM + Acyclovir |\n\n**Advantages of Syndromic Management**:\n* Immediate treatment without waiting for lab results (reduces transmission window).\n* Suitable for resource-limited, primary health settings.\n* Partner notification and treatment included.\n\n### C) NATIONAL AIDS CONTROL PROGRAMME (NACP) — STI CONTROL\n* **Targeted Interventions (TI)**: Providing STI services to high-risk groups (Female Sex Workers, MSM, IV drug users) through NGO-run drop-in centres.\n* **Link Worker Scheme**: Bridge population (truckers, migrants) outreach.\n* Free diagnosis and treatment of STIs at government facilities.",
