    "chapter": "Epidemiology of Communicable Diseases",
    "stars": 4,
    "answer": "### DIARRHEAL DISEASES & ORAL REHYDRATION\nDiarrhea is defined as the passage of three or more loose or watery stools per day.\n* **Etiology**: Rotavirus (most common in children), Vibrio cholerae, E. coli, Shigella.\n* **Management & Control**:\n  1. **Oral Rehydration Therapy (ORT)**: Using WHO low-osmolarity ORS to prevent dehydration.\n  2. **Zinc Supplementation**: $20\\text{ mg/day}$ for 10–14 days ($10\\text{ mg}$ for infants $<6$ months) to reduce diarrhea duration and severity.\n  3. **Breastfeeding & Nutrition**: Continued feeding during diarrhea.",
