    "text": "Preventive Measures Against Amoebiasis",
    "type": "SAQ",
    "chapter": "Epidemiology of Communicable Diseases",
    "stars": 4,
    "answer": "### AMOEBIASIS\nA parasitic infection of the large intestine caused by Entamoeba histolytica.\n* **Transmission**: Fecal-oral route via contaminated food or water containing mature cysts.\n* **Clinical Features**: Amoebic dysentery (stools with blood and mucus, abdominal pain, tenesmus) and hepatic complications (**Amoebic Liver Abscess** showing \"anchovy sauce\" pus).\n* **Prevention**: Protection of water supply from fecal contamination, sanitary disposal of excreta, and drug therapy (Metronidazole/Tinidazole).",
