    "text": "Write About Plague  & Flea Indices (Blocked Flea)",
    "type": "SAQ",
    "chapter": "Epidemiology of Communicable Diseases",
    "stars": 3,
    "answer": "### PLAGUE\nA severe zoonotic disease caused by Yersinia pestis.\n* **Transmission**: Bites of infected rat fleas (Xenopsylla cheopis) or inhalation of droplets.\n* **Clinical Types**: Bubonic (painful buboes in groin/axilla), Pneumonic (highly infectious droplet spread), and Septicemic (\"Black Death\").\n* **Control**: Vector control (DDT spraying), rodent control, and early treatment with Streptomycin, Gentamicin, or Doxycycline.",
