    "chapter": "Epidemiology of Non-Communicable Diseases",
    "stars": 6,
    "answer": "### CORONARY HEART DISEASE (CHD) / ISCHAEMIC HEART DISEASE (IHD)\n\n### A) EPIDEMIOLOGY\n* **Definition**: CHD is the result of myocardial ischaemia due to narrowing of the coronary arteries by atherosclerotic plaques.\n* **Global Burden**: Leading cause of death globally. India has one of the fastest rising CHD rates worldwide.\n* **Risk Factors**:\n  * **Non-Modifiable**: Increasing age, male sex (testosterone promotes atherosclerosis), family history, genetic predisposition.\n  * **Modifiable (Major)**: Hypertension, dyslipidaemia (high LDL, low HDL), cigarette smoking, diabetes mellitus, obesity (BMI >25 Asian cut-off).\n  * **Modifiable (Minor)**: Physical inactivity, stress/Type A personality, oral contraceptives, hyperuricaemia.\n\n### B) DIAGNOSIS\n* **ECG**: ST elevation (STEMI) or depression (NSTEMI), Q waves indicate infarction.\n* **Cardiac Biomarkers**: Troponin I/T (most specific and sensitive), CKMB, LDH.\n* **Echocardiography**: Assess regional wall motion abnormality, ejection fraction.\n* **Coronary Angiography**: Gold standard for visualising coronary artery stenosis.\n* **Lipid Profile**: Total cholesterol, LDL, HDL, triglycerides.\n\n### C) PREVENTION AND CONTROL\n* **Primordial Prevention**: Promoting healthy lifestyles in population before risk factors develop.\n* **Primary Prevention**: \n  * Regular aerobic exercise (≥150 min/week moderate intensity).\n  * Low-fat, high-fibre diet (Mediterranean diet pattern); reducing salt (<5 g/day).\n  * Complete cessation of smoking and alcohol.\n  * Regular monitoring of BP, blood sugar, and lipids.\n* **Secondary Prevention**: \n  * Anti-platelet therapy (**Aspirin 75–150 mg/day**), Statins (Atorvastatin), Beta-blockers, ACE inhibitors.\n  * **PTCA (Percutaneous Transluminal Coronary Angioplasty)** and coronary stenting.\n  * **CABG (Coronary Artery Bypass Grafting)** for multi-vessel disease.\n* **Tertiary Prevention**: Cardiac rehabilitation — structured exercise, psychological support, dietary counselling.\n\n### D) NATIONAL PROGRAMME\n* **NPCDCS** (National Programme for Prevention and Control of Cancer, Diabetes, Cardiovascular Diseases and Stroke) — screening, early detection, and management at CHC/DH level.",
