    "text": "CANCER: a) Epidemiology  And Danger Signals Of Cancer B) Prevention Of Cancers C) Add A Note On Prevention Of Oral Cancers And Cervix Cancer    (5+5+5) D) Cancer Registries",
    "type": "SAQ",
    "chapter": "Epidemiology of Non-Communicable Diseases",
    "stars": 3,
    "answer": "### CANCER EPIDEMIOLOGY AND CONTROL\n\n### A) EPIDEMIOLOGY\n* **Definition**: Cancer is a group of diseases characterised by uncontrolled, abnormal proliferation of cells that can invade adjacent tissues and spread to distant sites (metastasis).\n* **Burden in India**: India has ~1.4 million new cancer cases per year. Leading cancers: Oral/Head and Neck, Lung, Breast, Cervix, Stomach (males); Breast, Cervix, Ovary, Oral, Colorectal (females).\n* **Risk Factors**:\n  * *Biological*: Age, sex, hereditary mutations (BRCA1/2 for breast cancer).\n  * *Chemical carcinogens*: Tobacco (most important — causes 30% of all cancers), alcohol, aflatoxins, asbestos.\n  * *Physical carcinogens*: UV radiation (skin cancer), ionising radiation.\n  * *Viral*: HPV (cervical cancer), HBV/HCV (hepatocellular carcinoma), EBV (Burkitt's lymphoma), H. pylori (gastric cancer).\n\n### B) DANGER SIGNALS OF CANCER (CAUTION Mnemonic)\n* **C** — Change in bowel or bladder habits.\n* **A** — A sore that does not heal.\n* **U** — Unusual bleeding or discharge.\n* **T** — Thickening or lump in breast or elsewhere.\n* **I** — Indigestion or difficulty in swallowing.\n* **O** — Obvious change in a wart or mole.\n* **N** — Nagging cough or hoarseness of voice.\n\n### C) PREVENTION OF SPECIFIC CANCERS\n* **Cervical Cancer**: \n  * HPV vaccination (girls 9–14 years; Gardasil/Cervarix); 2 doses.\n  * Screening via Pap Smear (conventional) or **VIA (Visual Inspection with Acetic Acid)** — practical in Indian primary care settings.\n* **Oral/Oropharyngeal Cancer**:\n  * Complete cessation of tobacco (smoking and smokeless) and alcohol.\n  * Oral visual examination by ANM/health worker during field visits.\n* **Breast Cancer**: Self-Breast Examination (monthly), clinical breast examination, mammography.\n\n### D) NATIONAL PROGRAMME\n* **NPCDCS**: National Programme for Prevention and Control of Cancer, Diabetes, Cardiovascular Diseases and Stroke — provides cancer screening at District Hospital level.",
