    "text": "Road Traffic Accidents( RTA): A) Epidemiology B)Prevention And Control",
    "type": "SAQ",
    "chapter": "Epidemiology of Non-Communicable Diseases",
    "stars": 6,
    "answer": "### ROAD TRAFFIC ACCIDENTS (RTA)\n\n### A) EPIDEMIOLOGY\n* **Global**: RTAs kill ~1.35 million people annually worldwide (WHO). A leading cause of death in 5–29 year age group.\n* **India**: India has one of the world's highest RTA death rates — approximately 150,000 deaths per year.\n* **Time Distribution**: Peak between 6 PM–12 AM (reduced visibility, drunk driving).\n* **Place**: National and State Highways account for >50% of RTA deaths despite carrying only 5% of total traffic.\n* **Person Distribution**: Males 15–44 years are the most affected group. Motorcyclists (40%), pedestrians (20%), cyclists.\n\n**Contributory Factors (Haddon's Matrix)**:\n| | Pre-Crash | Crash | Post-Crash |\n|---|---|---|---|\n| **Human** | Drunk driving, speeding, fatigue, mobile phone use | Not wearing helmet/seatbelt | Delay in seeking help |\n| **Vehicle** | Brake failure, tyre blowout | Poor energy absorption | |\n| **Environment** | Poor road design, bad lighting | Sharp road features | Remote location, no trauma care |\n\n### B) PREVENTION AND CONTROL (4 E's)\n1. **Enforcement of Laws**: Mandatory helmet for 2-wheelers, seatbelts for 4-wheelers; speed limits; drunk-driving laws (BAC <30 mg/100 ml in India); red-light violations.\n2. **Engineering**:\n   * Road design improvements — crash barriers, rumble strips, pedestrian crossings.\n   * Vehicle design — air bags, anti-lock braking systems (ABS).\n3. **Education**: Road safety campaigns; traffic education in schools; promoting safe driving behaviour.\n4. **Emergency Care (\"Golden Hour\")**: Pre-hospital first aid by trained responders; establishing Level-1 Trauma Centres along national highways; National Trauma Management Protocol.\n\n### C) NATIONAL INITIATIVES\n* **SAVE LIFE FOUNDATION** and **MoRTH (Ministry of Road Transport and Highways)** initiatives.\n* \"Good Samaritan Law\" (Motor Vehicles Amendment Act 2019): Protects bystanders who help accident victims from legal liability.",
