    "id": 232,
    "text": "Rheumatic Fever Or Rheumatic Heart Disease: A) Epidemiology B) Diagnosis And Prevention.",
    "type": "SAQ",
    "chapter": "Epidemiology of Non-Communicable Diseases",
    "stars": 1,
    "answer": "### RHEUMATIC FEVER AND RHEUMATIC HEART DISEASE (RHD)\n\n### A) EPIDEMIOLOGY\n* **Agent**: Group A beta-haemolytic Streptococcus (*Streptococcus pyogenes*) — throat infection triggers rheumatic fever in susceptible individuals (autoimmune cross-reaction between streptococcal antigens and cardiac tissue).\n* **Host**: Children aged **5–15 years** are most susceptible.\n* **Environment**: Overcrowding, poor housing, cold climate — facilitating streptococcal throat infections.\n* **Latent Period**: Rheumatic fever develops **2–4 weeks** after streptococcal pharyngitis.\n* **Recurrence**: Each streptococcal infection in a person with rheumatic fever can trigger another attack, progressively damaging the heart valves.\n\n### B) DIAGNOSIS — JONES CRITERIA (2015 Revised AHA)\n**Diagnosis requires**: Confirmed streptococcal infection (elevated ASOT >200 IU, positive throat swab) **PLUS** 2 major criteria OR 1 major + 2 minor criteria.\n\n**Major Criteria (JONES)**:\n* **J** — Joints (Migratory Polyarthritis — most common)\n* **O** — (Heart) O-penness (Carditis — most serious)\n* **N** — Nodules (Subcutaneous nodules — Aschoff nodules)\n* **E** — Erythema Marginatum (skin rash — fleeting, non-pruritic)\n* **S** — Sydenham's Chorea (involuntary purposeless movements — \"St Vitus Dance\")\n\n**Minor Criteria**: Fever, Elevated ESR/CRP, prolonged PR interval on ECG.\n\n### C) PREVENTION AND CONTROL\n* **Primary Prevention**: Early diagnosis and COMPLETE TREATMENT of streptococcal pharyngitis with **Benzathine Penicillin G (BPG)** 1.2 million units IM single dose (or 10-day oral Penicillin V).\n* **Secondary Prevention (Prophylaxis)**: Long-term prophylaxis to prevent recurrence:\n  * **BPG 1.2 million units IM every 3–4 weeks** for 5–10 years (or until age 21, whichever is longer).\n  * Duration extended if active carditis or prosthetic heart valves.\n* **National Programme**: RHD control integrated under NCD prevention. School health screening for heart murmurs.",
