    "id": 240,
    "text": "Write about IUDs and its types",
    "type": "SAQ",
    "chapter": "Demography and Family Planning",
    "stars": 3,
    "answer": "### Intrauterine Devices (IUDs) and Their Types\n\nIntrauterine Devices (IUDs) are highly effective, long-acting, reversible contraceptive (LARC) spacing methods inserted into the uterine cavity by a trained healthcare provider.\n\n#### 1. First-Generation IUDs (Non-Medicated / Inert)\n*   **Description:** Made of non-reactive polyethylene or other inert materials. They do not contain active chemicals or hormones.\n*   **Mechanism:** Act as a mechanical foreign body, producing a local intrauterine inflammatory reaction that prevents implantation.\n*   **Example:** **Lippes Loop** (a double-S-shaped plastic device).\n*   *Advantage:* Can remain in place indefinitely (until menopause) if well tolerated. Currently, they have been largely replaced by second and third-generation devices.\n\n#### 2. Second-Generation IUDs (Medicated / Copper-Releasing)\n*   **Description:** Polyethylene T-shaped frame wrapped with fine copper wire or carrying copper sleeves.\n*   **Mechanism of Action:**\n    *   Copper ions are continuously released into the uterine cavity, acting as a highly effective **local spermicide**.\n    *   Copper impairs sperm motility, viability, and enzymatic activity, preventing fertilization.\n    *   It also alters the endometrial environment, preventing implantation.\n*   **Key Models:**\n    *   **Copper T 200:** Has 200 $\\text{mm}^2$ of copper surface area. Effective for 3 to 4 years.\n    *   **Copper T 380A:** The global gold standard. Features **380 $\\text{mm}^2$ of copper** (sleeves on horizontal arms and wire on the vertical stem). **Effective for 10 years** of continuous protection.\n    *   **Multiload 375 (ML-375):** Features flexible, serrated side arms to minimize expulsion rates. Effective for 5 years.\n\n#### 3. Third-Generation IUDs (Hormone-Releasing / Intrauterine Systems - IUS)\n*   **Description:** T-shaped plastic frame carrying a reservoir that slowly releases a low daily dose of a progestin.\n*   **Mechanism of Action:**\n    *   Continuous release of hormone causes profound **endometrial atrophy**, preventing implantation.\n    *   Thickens the cervical mucus to block sperm entry.\n    *   Reduces menstrual blood flow and cramps.\n*   **Examples:**\n    *   **Mirena (LNG-20):** Releases 20 mcg of **Levonorgestrel** daily. **Effective for 5 to 7 years**. Highly indicated as first-line treatment for menorrhagia and dysmenorrhea.\n    *   **Progestasert:** Releases progesterone; requires annual replacement.",
    "page": 26
