    "text": "SAHELI.",
    "type": "SAQ",
    "chapter": "Demography and Family Planning",
    "stars": 1,
    "answer": "### **Saheli (Centchroman / Ormeloxifene)**\n\n#### **1. Introduction**\n**Saheli** is the world’s first **non-steroidal, non-hormonal** oral contraceptive pill. It was researched and developed by the **Central Drug Research Institute (CDRI), Lucknow, India**, and is incorporated into the National Family Welfare Programme under the brand name **'Chhaya'**.\n\n#### **2. Composition & Mechanism of Action**\n*   **Active Ingredient**: **Centchroman (Ormeloxifene)**, 30 mg per tablet.\n*   **Mechanism**: It is a **Selective Estrogen Receptor Modulator (SERM)**. It exerts strong anti-estrogenic and weak estrogenic actions.\n    *   It accelerates zygote transport through the fallopian tube.\n    *   It alters the endometrial lining, rendering it hostile and non-receptive, thereby preventing blastocyst implantation (**nidation**).\n    *   It does not suppress ovulation, maintaining the natural menstrual and endocrine cycle.\n\n#### **3. Dosage Schedule**\nSaheli follows a unique, easy-to-remember administration schedule:\n*   **First 3 months**: One tablet **twice a week** (e.g., Sunday and Wednesday or Monday and Thursday) starting on Day 1 of the menstrual cycle.\n*   **Fourth month onwards**: One tablet **once a week** on the designated first day (e.g., every Sunday), regardless of menstrual flow.\n\n#### **4. Clinical Benefits & Advantages**\n*   **Excellent Safety Profile**: Being non-steroidal, it is completely free from classic steroid side effects (e.g., weight gain, nausea, acne, hirsutism, hepatotoxicity, hypertension, or changes in lipid profile).\n*   **Good Efficacy**: Low failure rate (Pearl Index: **1.2 to 1.83 pregnancies per 100 woman-years**).\n*   **Highly Reversible**: Conception can occur promptly upon discontinuation without residual delay in fertility.\n*   **Lactation Safe**: Does not interfere with the quality or quantity of breast milk, making it an excellent postpartum spacing option.\n\n#### **5. Side Effects**\n*   The primary side effect is a **mild delay in the menstrual cycle** (usually by 7–10 days in about 8% of cycles in the first few months), which is benign, non-pathological, and resolves spontaneously.",
