    "text": "MALA-N & MALA-D.",
    "type": "SAQ",
    "chapter": "Demography and Family Planning",
    "stars": 1,
    "answer": "### **Mala-N and Mala-D**\n\n#### **1. Introduction**\n**Mala-N** and **Mala-D** are low-dose, combined oral contraceptive pills (COCPs) widely used under the National Family Planning Programme in India.\n*   **Mala-N**: Provided **free of cost** at all government primary health centres, sub-centres, and hospitals.\n*   **Mala-D**: Distributed through **social marketing** channels at a highly subsidized nominal price.\n\n#### **2. Composition**\nEach active tablet contains:\n1.  **Ethinyl Estradiol**: **0.03 mg** (30 micrograms) – the estrogenic component.\n2.  **Levonorgestrel**: **0.15 mg** (150 micrograms) – the progestogenic component.\n\n#### **3. Packaging**\nEach calendar pack contains **28 tablets**:\n*   **21 white tablets**: Hormonal (active) pills.\n*   **7 brown tablets**: Contain **Ferrous Fumarate (60 mg)**. These pills serve two functions:\n    1.  Maintain the daily pill-taking routine during menses to prevent omission.\n    2.  Prophylactically treat and prevent iron-deficiency anemia in reproductive-age women.\n\n#### **4. Mechanism of Action**\n1.  **Prevents Ovulation**: Suppresses follicle-stimulating hormone (FSH) and luteinizing hormone (LH) secretion through negative feedback on the hypothalamus-pituitary axis.\n2.  **Thickens Cervical Mucus**: Makes the mucus thick, cellular, and highly viscous, preventing sperm penetration into the uterine cavity.\n3.  **Alters Endometrium**: Creates a thin, out-of-phase endometrial lining that is unreceptive to embryo implantation.\n\n#### **5. Usage Instructions & Missed Pill Rules**\n*   **Start**: Take the first white active pill on the **$1^{\\text{st}}$ day of the menstrual cycle** (no later than Day 5).\n*   **Routine**: One active pill daily at the same time for 21 days, followed by one brown iron pill daily for 7 days.\n*   **Missed Pill Protocol**:\n    *   *If 1 pill is missed*: Take it as soon as remembered, even if it means taking two pills in a single day.\n    *   *If 2 or more pills are missed*: Take the last missed pill immediately and continue the daily schedule, but use a backup spacing method (e.g., condoms) for the next 7 days.",
