    "id": 261,
    "text": "Add a note on First Referral unit for Safe Motherhood.",
    "type": "SAQ",
    "chapter": "SPM in Obs, Paeds, and Geriatrics",
    "stars": 4,
    "answer": "### **First Referral Unit (FRU) for Safe Motherhood**\n\n#### **1. Concept**\nA **First Referral Unit (FRU)** is an existing sub-district level healthcare facility (such as a Community Health Centre - CHC, Sub-District Hospital, or District Hospital) that has been upgraded and equipped to provide comprehensive, round-the-clock emergency obstetric and newborn care (EmONC) services. It serves as the primary referral link for sub-centres and Primary Health Centres (PHCs) within its catchment area.\n\n---\n\n#### **2. Mandatory Criteria for Declaration as an FRU**\nA health facility is not designated as an FRU merely based on its size, but only if it successfully provides three critical services **24 hours a day, 7 days a week**:\n\n1.  **Emergency Obstetric Care (EmOC)**: Fully functioning capability to perform emergency surgical interventions, including **Cesarean Sections**, and manage obstetric emergencies (e.g., ruptured uterus, severe pre-eclampsia/eclampsia, ectopic pregnancy).\n2.  **Neonatal/Newborn Care**: Capability to manage sick and low-birth-weight neonates through a dedicated **Newborn Stabilization Unit (NSU)** or Special Newborn Care Unit (SNCU).\n3.  **24-Hour Blood Storage Facility**: A fully licensed and operational blood storage center capable of arranging and storing blood for emergency transfusions.\n\n---\n\n#### **3. Human Resources and Infrastructure**\n*   **Specialist Team**: Requires the physical presence or 24/7 on-call availability of a multi-disciplinary team:\n    *   Obstetrician-Gynecologist\n    *   Pediatrician\n    *   Anesthetist\n    *   General Surgeon\n*   **Supportive Infrastructure**:\n    *   A fully equipped Emergency Operating Theatre (OT) and Labor Room (optimized under the **LaQshya** initiative).\n    *   Continuous supply of critical medicines: Oxytocin, Magnesium Sulfate (for eclampsia), Misoprostol, IV fluids, and emergency surgical kits.\n    *   Emergency transport links (102 and 108 ambulance services) to facilitate rapid transfer of patients from peripheral points and to tertiary centers if required.",
