    "id": 263,
    "text": "Write briefly on Under-5 clinic.",
    "type": "SAQ",
    "chapter": "SPM in Obs, Paeds, and Geriatrics",
    "stars": 3,
    "answer": "### **The Under-5 Clinic (Well Baby Clinic)**\n\n#### **1. Concept**\nThe **Under-5 Clinic** (historically established by David Morley) is a specialized facility where a comprehensive package of preventive, promotive, curative, and educational health services is provided to children under five years of age **under one roof**. This ensures that mothers do not have to visit multiple clinics for their child's various health and nutritional needs.\n\n---\n\n#### **2. Symbol of the Under-5 Clinic**\nThe clinic is symbolized by a **large triangle** containing four smaller triangles inside, surrounded by an outer circular or triangular border. Each part represents a specific service component:\n\n```\n               /\\\n              /  \\\n             /    \\\n            / Cur. \\\n           /________\\\n          /\\        /\\\n         /  \\  FP  /  \\\n        / GM \\    /Prev\\\n       /______\\__/______\\\n      (   Health Education   )\n```\n\n1.  **The Apex (Top Triangle) – Care in Illness**:\n    *   Represents curative services. Provides diagnosis and immediate treatment for common pediatric illnesses (diarrhea, pneumonia, malaria, ear infections, skin conditions).\n2.  **The Left Base Triangle – Growth Monitoring**:\n    *   Represents tracking child growth. Children are weighed regularly (monthly during the 1st year, every 2 months in the 2nd year, and quarterly thereafter). Weights are plotted on the **WHO Growth Chart** to detect early growth faltering and protein-energy malnutrition (PEM) before clinical signs manifest.\n3.  **The Right Base Triangle – Preventive Care**:\n    *   Focuses on immunizations according to the National Immunization Schedule, administering **Vitamin A prophylaxis** (9 doses from 9 months to 5 years), iron-folic acid distribution, and regular deworming.\n4.  **The Central Triangle – Family Planning**:\n    *   Serves as a direct link to maternal health. Parents are counseled on spacing methods, limiting family size, and reproductive health, emphasizing that healthy spacing (at least 3 years) directly improves child survival rates.\n5.  **The Outer Border – Health Education**:\n    *   Encompasses all four triangles. It represents continuous health education given to mothers regarding exclusive breastfeeding, sanitary hygiene, home-made complementary foods, and recognizing danger signs of illness.",
