    "id": 275,
    "text": "Describe ERGONOMICS .(Definition and examples).",
    "type": "SAQ",
    "chapter": "Occupational Health",
    "stars": 3,
    "answer": "### ERGONOMICS\nErgonomics is the study of designing the work environment, equipment, and tasks to fit the capabilities of the worker (\"fitting the job to the worker\").\n* **Goal**: Reduce occupational injuries (MSDs, back pain), improve safety, and maximize productivity.",
