    "text": "a)Vision 2020: Right to Sight b)Salient features of National Programme for Control of Blindness",
    "type": "LAQ",
    "chapter": "Health Programmes in India",
    "stars": 4,
    "answer": "### BLINDNESS & VISION 2020\n* **Definition (WHO)**: Visual acuity of less than $3/60$ in the better eye with best possible correction.\n* **Causes in India**: **Cataract (~62%)**, refractive errors, glaucoma, diabetic retinopathy, corneal xerosis (vitamin A deficiency).\n* **Vision 2020: The Right to Sight**: WHO global joint initiative to eliminate avoidable blindness. Main targets: Cataract, refractive errors, childhood blindness, trachoma.",
