    "answer": "### DIDACTIC VS SOCRATIC METHODS\n* **Didactic Method (One-way / Lecture)**: Passive; teacher talks, students listen. Minimal feedback. Good for delivering quick facts to large groups, but poor at changing habits.\n* **Socratic Method (Two-way / Discussion)**: Active; continuous dialogue and questions between teacher and students. Immediate feedback. Excellent for critical thinking and changing attitudes.",
